WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.443
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.713 --> 00:01.713
Miyata?

3
00:06.459 --> 00:07.747
And the payment?

4
00:08.632 --> 00:10.735
I took care of it all.

5
00:12.200 --> 00:13.388
So...

6
00:17.442 --> 00:18.895
don't worry.

7
00:18.895 --> 00:20.786
But...

8
00:20.786 --> 00:21.786
Hm?

9
00:23.603 --> 00:25.698
I want to pay half too.

10
00:25.698 --> 00:29.551
Then how about you pay me a monthly amount?

11
00:29.551 --> 00:31.949
I'll put it in both our names.

12
00:31.949 --> 00:35.786
Wouldn't that incur a gift tax?

13
00:35.786 --> 00:40.350
See? I love how sharp you are.

14
00:40.350 --> 00:42.636
Don't change the subject.

15
00:42.636 --> 00:43.636
Sorry.

16
00:44.961 --> 00:47.506
Besides, why would you buy this?

17
00:51.013 --> 00:53.994
With this contract,

18
00:54.979 --> 00:57.432
I wanted to give shape to my feelings for you.

19
00:59.273 --> 01:03.689
But you might change your mind, right?

20
01:04.632 --> 01:05.733
I won't.

21
01:07.981 --> 01:10.654
You might regret paying the full amount.

22
01:11.991 --> 01:14.741
I never will.

23
01:17.765 --> 01:21.312
So I want you to believe in me.

24
01:26.869 --> 01:30.203
I still can't move in.

25
01:31.565 --> 01:33.766
Not until I can properly contribute too.

26
01:36.950 --> 01:40.016
I guess I got ahead of myself.

27
02:23.091 --> 02:24.891
I know what I said,

28
02:24.891 --> 02:29.090
but earning as much as Senpai could take a while.

29
02:32.174 --> 02:34.021
Editor-in-chief,

30
02:34.021 --> 02:37.102
I've shared the rough design of Prof. Iwanaga's book.

31
02:37.102 --> 02:38.308
Got it.

32
02:40.176 --> 02:42.768
This looks good.

33
02:42.768 --> 02:44.435
Could be a hit, huh?

34
02:44.435 --> 02:47.060
Then give us a big bonus.

35
02:47.060 --> 02:48.060
Okay, okay.

36
02:48.856 --> 02:51.201
Hello, do you all have a moment?

37
02:52.391 --> 02:55.317
Um, as you all probably know,

38
02:55.317 --> 02:58.943
our company has had consultants working with us for six months,

39
02:58.943 --> 03:01.264
pushing forward with company reform.

40
03:01.264 --> 03:06.644
And at this stage, they'll be working with Business Now too.

41
03:06.644 --> 03:08.271
Let me introduce you.

42
03:08.271 --> 03:09.271
Masumoto, please.

43
03:11.918 --> 03:15.035
I'm Yuko Masumoto from Veritas Partners.

44
03:15.035 --> 03:18.259
I'll be starting here tomorrow. It's nice to meet you.

45
03:19.980 --> 03:21.166
Nice to meet you.

46
03:34.093 --> 03:38.968
Even when work gets rough, I get to come home to Senpai.

47
03:42.651 --> 03:43.651
Welcome back.

48
03:46.136 --> 03:51.648
I thought your looks were natural, but it actually takes effort, huh?

49
03:53.942 --> 03:58.805
Want to join in, Miyata? It's about time you started caring.

50
03:58.805 --> 04:00.725
My body doesn't gain weight.

51
04:01.441 --> 04:05.499
That's what I said too, until a year ago.

52
04:05.499 --> 04:08.498
Middle age comes to you before you know it.

53
04:09.759 --> 04:11.752
I'm two years younger, so I'm fine.

54
04:18.951 --> 04:23.248
What brought this about? You went all-out on this meal.

55
04:23.248 --> 04:25.449
I wanted to make you happy, Miyata.

56
04:31.771 --> 04:35.367
Organic tomatoes and Yonezawa beef.

57
04:36.978 --> 04:39.529
You went to that expensive supermarket again.

58
04:41.384 --> 04:42.529
Is that bad?

59
04:45.244 --> 04:48.276
Cheap stuff is fine. Cheap stuff.

60
04:49.242 --> 04:51.416
We need to save for our old age.

61
04:54.565 --> 04:55.617
All right.

62
04:57.660 --> 04:59.688
What are we making today?

63
04:59.688 --> 05:03.434
Today, I'm making caprese. Your favorite, Miyata.

64
05:03.434 --> 05:04.434
Oh?

65
05:06.968 --> 05:08.452
Does this look okay?

66
05:08.452 --> 05:11.565
A little more. Smash a bit more.

67
05:13.173 --> 05:14.189
Yes, like that.

68
05:20.695 --> 05:22.197
Careful, I'm cutting!

69
05:23.440 --> 05:26.251
- Okay, keep cutting. - Okay, here goes.

70
05:30.463 --> 05:31.587
How was today?

71
05:32.994 --> 05:34.691
You mean work?

72
05:34.691 --> 05:35.691
Yeah.

73
05:37.635 --> 05:39.964
Nothing special. Same as always.

74
05:43.462 --> 05:45.094
You look troubled though.

75
05:48.269 --> 05:51.239
Maybe the ingredients are so fancy,

76
05:51.239 --> 05:52.878
my stomach's in shock.

77
05:57.482 --> 06:01.739
These are Business Now's recent sales figures.

78
06:01.739 --> 06:05.516
Both magazine and book sales are trending downward.

79
06:05.516 --> 06:11.343
As you know, the entire publishing industry is on its last legs.

80
06:11.343 --> 06:14.012
There's no point in just lamenting the situation.

81
06:16.416 --> 06:19.481
The question is how we fight.

82
06:19.481 --> 06:22.245
I want to think about that together with all of you.

83
06:24.767 --> 06:25.781
Miyata.

84
06:26.554 --> 06:27.830
Yes.

85
06:27.830 --> 06:29.331
What project are you working on?

86
06:30.661 --> 06:35.186
Well, I'm producing a book on exploring new forms of business

87
06:35.186 --> 06:39.335
with Associate Professor Takashi Iwanaga at Toou University.

88
06:39.335 --> 06:40.592
How are you promoting it?

89
06:41.989 --> 06:46.965
We're asking prominent academics for endorsement blurbs,

90
06:46.965 --> 06:49.447
and aiming for at least two newspaper reviews...

91
06:49.447 --> 06:50.447
Stop.

92
06:52.019 --> 06:56.921
Young people today are reading less and less.

93
06:56.921 --> 07:00.921
So where are they getting their information?

94
07:02.791 --> 07:04.596
Video?

95
07:04.596 --> 07:06.092
Exactly.

96
07:07.510 --> 07:11.336
Submit a video promotion proposal by tomorrow.

97
07:11.336 --> 07:12.336
Tomorrow?

98
07:14.938 --> 07:16.836
- Here. - Okay.

99
07:16.836 --> 07:19.555
Then I'll keep this in the reference shelf.

100
07:19.555 --> 07:20.674
Okay, thanks.

101
07:21.494 --> 07:26.346
Shiraishi, is there a cheap supermarket around here?

102
07:27.709 --> 07:29.170
Cheap?

103
07:29.170 --> 07:30.422
Yeah.

104
07:30.422 --> 07:33.811
Cheap? Bargains? Good deals?

105
07:35.218 --> 07:36.414
Why do you ask?

106
07:37.251 --> 07:41.753
Miyata scolded me for always buying expensive ingredients.

107
07:46.778 --> 07:49.678
That little...

108
07:50.440 --> 07:51.440
Hm?

109
07:55.147 --> 07:57.545
In that case, Asahi Supermarket.

110
07:57.545 --> 08:00.163
Go out the main gate and head straight.

111
08:01.214 --> 08:03.554
Thanks. You're a big help.

112
08:05.474 --> 08:08.407
Asahi Supermarket, huh?

113
08:17.024 --> 08:18.686
I'm home.

114
08:18.686 --> 08:19.821
Welcome back.

115
08:21.780 --> 08:24.200
Today, I bought reasonably priced ingredients.

116
08:25.270 --> 08:26.327
Pea sprouts.

117
08:28.282 --> 08:29.282
Bean sprouts.

118
08:31.106 --> 08:32.721
And discounted chicken.

119
08:33.813 --> 08:36.391
I have to finish a proposal by tomorrow.

120
08:41.219 --> 08:44.848
Okay... I see.

121
08:48.087 --> 08:52.747
Then I'll put yours in the fridge, so eat it later, okay?

122
08:53.788 --> 08:55.118
Sorry.

123
09:12.157 --> 09:13.636
Come sit here for a moment.

124
09:31.487 --> 09:35.992
Why do you do so much for me?

125
09:37.173 --> 09:39.037
Because you seem busy lately.

126
09:42.161 --> 09:44.319
Do I look overwhelmed?

127
09:44.319 --> 09:45.460
You do.

128
09:48.991 --> 09:50.613
Whoa.

129
09:50.613 --> 09:52.141
Is it helping?

130
09:52.141 --> 09:53.176
So much.

131
09:55.767 --> 09:58.890
I wish I could press the pressure points in your heart.

132
10:05.609 --> 10:07.232
You can rely on me. Don't be shy.

133
10:21.540 --> 10:25.279
Actually, a consultant came to our department.

134
10:25.279 --> 10:26.484
Oh, really?

135
10:28.044 --> 10:32.376
I was suddenly ordered to make a video.

136
10:32.376 --> 10:33.760
A video?

137
10:33.760 --> 10:37.036
Like a video where I interview you...

138
10:38.233 --> 10:39.473
Of course I'll do it.

139
10:41.722 --> 10:43.999
I'd really appreciate it,

140
10:45.193 --> 10:47.268
but I don't want to be on camera.

141
10:49.320 --> 10:52.244
I'm not good at standing in front of people,

142
10:52.244 --> 10:55.263
let alone having a video of me stay online forever.

143
10:58.081 --> 10:59.492
Hmm.

144
11:01.327 --> 11:02.327
In that case...

145
11:05.493 --> 11:06.493
Huh?

146
11:18.690 --> 11:22.668
Hotta, since when did you have such a nice camera?

147
11:22.668 --> 11:24.738
I used to do video work.

148
11:24.738 --> 11:26.567
I even worked part-time at a TV station.

149
11:26.567 --> 11:27.670
Wow!

150
11:33.722 --> 11:35.695
Camera crew, standing by!

151
11:50.643 --> 11:51.982
Am I in the shot?

152
11:51.982 --> 11:53.684
We'll cut it later, so it's fine.

153
11:55.395 --> 11:57.027
Okay, ready.

154
11:57.027 --> 12:00.345
Rolling in three, two...

155
12:05.081 --> 12:06.466
Hello!

156
12:06.466 --> 12:08.861
My name is Biz-Bear!

157
12:09.563 --> 12:15.586
Today, on Biz-Bear's Classroom, I'm introducing this hot-off-the-press book,

158
12:16.377 --> 12:19.072
"Searching for Tomorrow's Value"!

159
12:20.826 --> 12:22.059
And the author is...

160
12:23.190 --> 12:27.710
the man with a smile as sweet as strawberry shortcake,

161
12:27.710 --> 12:32.083
Takashi Iwanaga, Associate Professor at Toou University!

162
12:32.083 --> 12:34.612
I'm Iwanaga. Nice to meet you.

163
12:35.500 --> 12:37.324
Hey, Professor,

164
12:37.324 --> 12:41.312
is this book too hard for me?

165
12:41.312 --> 12:44.876
No, it's written in simple language,

166
12:44.876 --> 12:47.333
so even you can read it easily, Biz-Bear.

167
12:55.488 --> 12:58.686
Miyata, Biz-Bear is so cute!

168
12:58.686 --> 13:00.529
Oh, thank you.

169
13:06.976 --> 13:07.976
You were cute.

170
13:10.156 --> 13:11.156
Thanks.

171
13:15.963 --> 13:19.418
You've been wearing that watch a lot lately.

172
13:19.418 --> 13:21.676
The other one broke.

173
13:23.301 --> 13:24.301
I see.

174
13:29.553 --> 13:31.394
Three, two...

175
13:34.044 --> 13:36.652
Okay! I have a question, Professor!

176
13:36.652 --> 13:38.095
What is it?

177
13:38.095 --> 13:41.696
What is "market re-entry"?

178
13:41.696 --> 13:47.069
It's when a company that once withdrew comes back into the same market again.

179
13:47.069 --> 13:49.509
Why do they come back?

180
13:49.509 --> 13:53.016
Well, the market environment changes,

181
13:53.016 --> 13:56.611
rival companies go under, or all sorts of other reasons.

182
13:59.284 --> 14:00.284
Let's start over.

183
14:01.466 --> 14:05.316
Now that we're both done chasing our careers,

184
14:05.316 --> 14:06.763
we can face each other properly.

185
14:09.417 --> 14:10.772
- Here? - Yeah, great.

186
14:16.015 --> 14:19.348
But it also costs money,

187
14:19.348 --> 14:23.946
and regaining something you once lost isn't that easy, is it?

188
14:25.897 --> 14:28.392
When the re-entering side is strong,

189
14:28.392 --> 14:32.527
if the existing players haven't built a solid foundation,

190
14:32.527 --> 14:34.690
they might end up losing.

191
14:44.641 --> 14:46.332
That got a little too complicated.

192
14:48.267 --> 14:49.346
Let's reshoot it.

193
14:50.412 --> 14:51.412
Okay.

194
14:57.162 --> 14:58.565
Glad it went well.

195
15:00.065 --> 15:01.692
Thanks to you, Professor Iwanaga.

196
15:11.823 --> 15:16.080
Oh, cleanup looks like it'll take a while, so go ahead.

197
15:16.080 --> 15:17.080
I see.

198
15:17.847 --> 15:20.107
I was gonna go shopping before heading home.

199
15:21.506 --> 15:23.089
There's something I'm looking for.

200
15:25.831 --> 15:28.678
I see. I'll see you later.

201
15:32.410 --> 15:33.410
Yeah.

202
15:38.485 --> 15:40.815
- I'll head off first. - Thank you.

203
16:41.345 --> 16:42.553
A video?

204
16:44.462 --> 16:48.933
Looks like Hasegawa's taken a new approach after I quit.

205
16:48.933 --> 16:52.706
Even the editor-in-chief is just doing it because the consultant said to.

206
16:52.706 --> 16:55.283
A consultant, huh?

207
16:55.283 --> 16:56.925
Since I went freelance,

208
16:56.925 --> 16:59.844
I don't have people sticking their noses in anymore.

209
16:59.844 --> 17:02.831
It's tough, but freeing in its own way.

210
17:02.831 --> 17:07.020
You're better suited to working freely, Seki.

211
17:07.020 --> 17:08.302
Unlike me.

212
17:09.267 --> 17:10.351
Who knows?

213
17:13.037 --> 17:15.996
Actually, I got married recently.

214
17:15.996 --> 17:16.996
What?

215
17:17.736 --> 17:19.246
Congratulations!

216
17:20.375 --> 17:22.876
I debated whether to go back to the company,

217
17:22.876 --> 17:25.967
but in the end, I decided to keep at it.

218
17:28.322 --> 17:29.322
What about you?

219
17:30.682 --> 17:31.682
Me?

220
17:33.404 --> 17:35.042
Are you dating? Getting married?

221
17:37.881 --> 17:39.162
Was that inappropriate?

222
17:41.473 --> 17:45.230
Well, it's not like we're coworkers anymore, so...

223
17:45.230 --> 17:46.230
Right.

224
17:47.420 --> 17:49.139
Um...

225
17:51.199 --> 17:52.237
I have someone.

226
17:53.539 --> 17:54.756
We're living together.

227
17:57.482 --> 17:59.537
So, maybe someday?

228
18:03.044 --> 18:04.625
Yeah, someday.

229
18:09.005 --> 18:14.908
Well, let's both do our best to stay happy for the long haul.

230
18:16.213 --> 18:17.213
Yeah.

231
18:18.765 --> 18:20.611
- Cheers. - Cheers.

232
18:46.219 --> 18:49.670
I wonder if we can stay happy for the long haul.

233
19:33.255 --> 19:35.425
My name is Biz-Bear.

234
19:36.948 --> 19:42.436
This video is our company's book introduction program using Biz-Bear.

235
19:42.436 --> 19:46.003
Going forward, we plan to bring in high-quality equipment

236
19:46.003 --> 19:50.084
and create an original plush character for filming.

237
19:50.084 --> 19:53.526
Part of it is Professor Iwanaga's charm,

238
19:53.526 --> 19:56.971
but you have an unexpected talent for this, Miyata.

239
19:58.097 --> 19:59.097
Not at all.

240
20:00.750 --> 20:05.670
Eventually, we plan to develop Biz-Bear into our company's IP.

241
20:05.670 --> 20:07.736
I see. An IP.

242
20:09.357 --> 20:11.549
Then why not do the same with the book?

243
20:12.759 --> 20:13.984
Huh?

244
20:13.984 --> 20:16.976
Restructure Professor Iwanaga's book

245
20:16.976 --> 20:20.697
and make it the first installment of the "Biz-Bear Classroom" series?

246
20:20.697 --> 20:24.164
Wait a moment. You can't just decide that on your own.

247
20:25.275 --> 20:30.870
Director Tanabe gave me full authority over this department's operations.

248
20:35.937 --> 20:40.310
But we've spent half a year on this book,

249
20:41.866 --> 20:45.300
and I have a relationship of trust with Professor Iwanaga.

250
20:45.300 --> 20:48.706
I'll be sure to explain to the professor.

251
20:55.268 --> 20:56.268
Hasegawa.

252
20:58.417 --> 21:01.370
Is that decision set in stone?

253
21:01.370 --> 21:04.847
No, I'll try talking to the higher-ups too.

254
21:05.914 --> 21:07.950
Thank you.

255
21:07.950 --> 21:12.271
But honestly, I think it'll be pretty tough.

256
21:13.648 --> 21:14.648
Huh?

257
21:16.485 --> 21:21.430
Maybe they don't need us in this company anymore.

258
21:25.689 --> 21:27.452
Might want to go independent.

259
22:04.072 --> 22:05.072
Welcome back.

260
22:10.278 --> 22:12.694
Um...

261
22:13.519 --> 22:16.045
I should've done this before buying the condo.

262
22:18.109 --> 22:21.799
I really want to make sure I'm the one who does this.

263
22:24.320 --> 22:25.320
Do what?

264
22:26.454 --> 22:28.022
I told you a long time ago,

265
22:29.218 --> 22:31.035
you can't measure love physically.

266
22:32.027 --> 22:33.027
Do you remember?

267
22:35.645 --> 22:37.737
You might have said that.

268
22:39.725 --> 22:41.418
I take it back.

269
22:44.573 --> 22:48.432
I want you to feel the weight of my love.

270
22:55.169 --> 22:56.515
On your ring finger.

271
23:09.544 --> 23:10.878
Akihiro Miyata,

272
23:12.671 --> 23:15.019
will you be my life partner?

273
23:30.988 --> 23:31.988
I'm sorry!

274
23:45.388 --> 23:48.400
Maybe we both grew up too much.

275
23:48.400 --> 23:49.199
Long time no see.

276
23:49.199 --> 23:50.686
Were you two dating?

277
23:50.686 --> 23:54.726
There can be a second time too, like for us.

278
23:54.726 --> 23:56.591
But I love you so much.

279
23:56.591 --> 23:59.520
Please just forget about me.
